{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Avraham went with them to send them off.</b> And immediately after it is written ״וַה׳ אָמַר״ — and HaShem said — and its meaning is that He said to Avraham, that by the merit of the escort the prophetic speech came to him. And the measure of the commandment of escorting (לויה), our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: a fellow to a fellow until the edge of the city; a teacher to a student until the Sabbath boundary (תחום שבת); a student to a teacher three parasangs; a host to a guest one mil, as is said (Psalms 91:11): ״כִּי מַלְאָכָיו יְצַוֶּה לָּךְ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:20.331638997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}